    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17083" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">explōrātōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		explorator, II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to searching
				out</i>, <i>exploratory</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coronae,</span>”
				<i>a reward for scouts or those who sought out and
						pursued the enemy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scaphae,</span>”
				<i>spy-boats</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 5, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
